INT. LEGAL AID OFFICE, FORMER DENTIST'S SUITE - EVENING

A reception desk with a dental chair behind it, used as a client seat. Beige carpet. A dusty fish tank. Diplomas of a man who is no longer here.

Four people around a conference table made of two card tables pushed together.

ATTORNEY OLIVIA OYELARAN-BRENNAN (40s, cardigan, reading glasses on her head). PARALEGAL MARCO TRAN-ASHWORTH (20s, laptop). CLIENT HAROLD BEAUMONT-ADEYEMI (60s, an old coat, scarred hands). INTERPRETER LUCIA FERREIRA-DAS (50s, a notebook).

OLIVIA
Mr. Beaumont-Adeyemi, I'd like to go through the eviction notice again.

HAROLD
I've read it.

OLIVIA
I know. But I'd like to hear what you think it says.

HAROLD
It says I owe four months.

OLIVIA
Do you?

HAROLD
I paid in cash.

MARCO
Do you have receipts?

HAROLD
She wrote them by hand.

OLIVIA
Who is "she"?

HAROLD
Mrs. Okonkwo. The landlady.

LUCIA
(translating)
La casera. Okonkwo.

OLIVIA
Do you have copies?

HAROLD
She keeps the originals. I keep the carbon.

MARCO
Carbon copies?

HAROLD
I'm sixty-three, young man.

MARCO
I'm sorry.

HAROLD
Don't be. They were the best thing she ever did for me.

OLIVIA
Where are the carbons?

HAROLD
In the freezer.

OLIVIA
The freezer?

HAROLD
That's where I keep the important things.

LUCIA
(to Olivia, aside)
He means it.

OLIVIA
Can you bring them tomorrow?

HAROLD
Bring them? I'd have to defrost them.

MARCO
That's allowed.

HAROLD
Is it?

OLIVIA
Mr. Beaumont-Adeyemi, you are going to win this case.

HAROLD
You haven't seen the carbons.

OLIVIA
I don't need to.

HAROLD
Why not?

OLIVIA
Because the notice names the wrong tenant.

Harold blinks. Marco looks up. Lucia stops writing.

HAROLD
What?

OLIVIA
It says "Beaumont-Adeyemi, Harold J." Your middle initial is R.

HAROLD
That's my brother's.

OLIVIA
Then they're evicting your brother.

HAROLD
(slowly)
He's been dead since 'ninety-four.

OLIVIA
Then they're evicting a ghost.
